Fix NCollection_Array1 constructor ambiguity with OCCT 8.0.0.

OCCT 8.0.0 adds an NCollection_Array1(pointer, size_t) buffer-reuse
constructor. With a literal 0 lower bound (a null-pointer constant), calls
like `TColgp_Array1OfPnt poles(0, vpoles.size()-1)` become ambiguous between
the (int, int) and (pointer, size_t) constructors. Cast the arguments to
Standard_Integer so the (int, int) constructor is selected unambiguously.

This is on top of the upstream "fixes for compatibility with occ 8.0" change
(occt8-compat.patch); those lines are not addressed there.

diff --git a/libsrc/occ/python_occ_shapes.cpp b/libsrc/occ/python_occ_shapes.cpp
index 8703f4d..ba12efe 100644
